```

7. Update the `scripts` section of your `package.json` file to include the following:

```json
"scripts": {
  "start": "electron .",
  "package": "electron-packager . --overwrite --asar=true --icon=icon.ico --prune=true --out=builds --version=1.0.0 --name=MyApp --version-string.CompanyName=MyCompany --version-string.ProductName=MyApp --version-string.FileDescription=MyApp"
}
```

8. Create an icon file named `icon.ico` in your project directory. You can use any icon editor to create this file.

9. Now you can start your application by running:

```bash
npm start
```

10. To package your application for distribution, run:

```bash
npm run package
```

This will create a distributable package of your application in the `builds` folder.

